status: wip
date: 2026-11-11
nixpkgs: nixos-26.05 (see flake.lock; unchanged from 0/3/0)
changes: Patch (fixes only), D-017 — lessons from bnox-bg/agenthub, the first real 0/3/0 consumer. (1) Thing manifest vs code sources split made explicit: `source` is where .bnox/ is read at eval (a locked flake input — pure flake eval cannot see /srv, G20; the documented source = "/srv/<thing>" never worked under nixos-rebuild --flake); code is built from /srv/<name> as before. The build unit warns when /srv/<name>/.bnox differs from the evaluated manifest. (2) Build unit fixes (all verified live on agenthub as host-side overrides): /etc/gitconfig safe.directory per thing checkout (nix's libgit2 ignores -c, G21); XDG_CACHE_HOME=/var/lib/<name>/.cache (fetcher cache under ProtectHome=read-only, G22); ReadWritePaths + /run/lock /run/libpod /run/containers /var/cache/containers (podman, G24) and /nix/var/log/nix (first local build, G31); the same-sha tar is removed before podman save (cannot overwrite, G25 — only that file, the older tars are the rollback set). (3) Sync unit IPAddressAllow ":443 :22 :53" was load-invalid on systemd 260 (same class as D-016 §5, missed in 0/3/0) → any. (4) Host-install units load their slots as EnvironmentFile (nats_seed required, other slots "-"-prefixed), as the container runtime already did (G28); their secrets dir is no longer writable. (5) The file secrets backend creates every declared slot as an empty root:root 0600 file (tmpfiles f — never rewrites; podman refuses to start on a missing env file). (6) pkgs.system → pkgs.stdenv.hostPlatform.system (eval deprecation warning). Upgrade note for hosts that pre-created slot files with their own tmpfiles lines: drop them — duplicate tmpfiles lines keep only the first (bnox's, empty), so a value carried in a host line would be lost on a fresh install. Eval-verified against agenthub (bnox-bg) via --override-input; not yet deployed (done rule, D-017 §6).
